From e5d678169c052940009201338af7832fdc672ca2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vadim Pasternak <vadimp@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Dec 2025 19:18:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] hwmon: (pmbus/mp5926): Add support for device MP5926

Add support for MPS device MP5926.

The MP5926 is a high voltage hot-swap controller capable of operating
with supplies 8V to 80V. The MP5926 provides a controlled soft start
during hot insertion to ensure a controlled output voltage ramp occurs.

Write PAGE 0 at probe: the device may have been left on a non-zero page
and, with .pages = 1, the PMBus core never programs PAGE itself.

EFUSE_CFG bit 12 selects the telemetry format. When set, all quantities
are linear11: the driver keeps the unsigned 11-bit READ_VOUT mantissa
and reports the exponent read at probe through VOUT_MODE. Otherwise the
direct format is used, and the input current coefficient is changed
when I_SCALE_SEL bit 6 is set.

Signed-off-by: Vadim Pasternak <vadimp@nvidia.com>

Upstream-Status: Pending [modified from mainline ca2cf3554492]

---
